{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-pillow-2026-112894",
  "summary": "Pillow: Quadratic-time DoS in PDF save_all (PdfParser.next_object_id)",
  "details": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. From 5.1.0 until 13.0.0, Pillow takes quadratic time to reserve PDF object identifiers when saving many frames with save_all enabled. PdfParser.next_object_id() repeatedly rebuilds and scans all previously reserved identifiers for every object. An attacker can supply a multi-frame image, including a small APNG with a large declared frame count, to an application that converts it to a multipage PDF. This can consume excessive CPU and deny service. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0.",
